// run_target7_chains — global initializers that read an object's member (plain, `?.`, `??`), declared above
// and below the object, applied at startup; `?.` member increments used as values and as
// statements; and an ancestor cast before `?.` on a method call.
// EXPECT_OUTPUT: 3 alpha al unnamed 3 alpha 0 1 2 2 3 1 2 node node
#beguilerSettings { target = z5; informName = "none"; }
int EarlyPri = nodeA.Pri;
string EarlyTitle = nodeA?.Title;
string EarlyNick = nodeA.Nick ?? "al";
string MissNick = nodeB.Nick ?? "unnamed";
class Node : object {
    int Pri = 3;
    int Hits;
    string Title;
    string Nick;
    default string Kind() { return "node"; }
}
class Leaf : Node {
    replace string Kind() { return "leaf"; }
}
Node nodeA { Title = "alpha"; Nick = "al"; }
Node nodeB { }
Leaf leafB { }
int LatePri = nodeA.Pri;
string LateTitle = nodeA?.Title;
void main() {
    bglInit();
    print(EarlyPri); print(" "); print(EarlyTitle); print(" "); print(EarlyNick); print(" "); print(MissNick); print(" ");
    print(LatePri); print(" "); print(LateTitle); print(" ");
    int was = nodeA?.Hits++;
    print(was); print(" "); print(nodeA.Hits); print(" ");
    int pre = ++nodeA?.Hits;
    print(pre); print(" "); print(nodeA.Hits); print(" ");
    nodeA?.Hits++;
    print(nodeA.Hits); print(" ");
    nodeA.Hits = 1;
    print(nodeA?.Hits++); print(" "); print(nodeA.Hits); print(" ");
    print(((Node)leafB).Kind()); print(" "); print(((Node)leafB)?.Kind());
}
